§9.1/D-10 rule 3 (S2-5.2): a decorator that no pass in the chain will ever claim
is **removed with a `Warning`**. It never renders as a stray `@@…` line, and it
never decorates a block it does not own.

The block can never receive a decorator at all (a thematic break):

@@{.nowhere}
---

The block belongs to a receiver this chain does not have — `plugin` is
`markdown` only, so `section`, `table`, `list` and `blockquote` are absent:

@@{.nope}
## A heading that gets no decorator

@@{.nope}
- a list that gets no decorator

@@{.nope}
> a quote that gets no decorator

@@{.nope}
| A |
| --- |
| 1 |

Two decorator lines in a row: only the last one applies, so the first is
overridden and dropped (`Overridden`):

@@first{.a}
@@second{.b}
A paragraph that keeps only `second`.
